{"law_id": "customer-sale", "says": "A sale transfers boxed pencils from the shop to the customer and pays the shop from the customer's cash.", "move": "sell-boxes", "gives": {"resource": "boxed-pencils", "from": "shop", "to": "customer"}, "pays": {"resource": "cash", "from": "customer", "to": "shop"}}]}"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Rules were written for that structure and test-run, and this is what happened: A separate check read your rules against the description and the laws and found: assemble pencil units: The move consumes paint, erasers, and ferrules and produces unboxed pencils, but none of these are defined as resources in the world's laws, so the move will be refused. (the description says: "paints them and adds erasers and brass ferrules") nothing in the rules: The chain is supposed to keep running, but there is no rule or process that supplies the factory with paint, erasers, ferrules, or empty boxes, meaning the factory will eventually halt. (the description says: "paints them and adds erasers and brass ferrules, packs them into boxes") make leads from materials: The move consumes graphite and clay, which are not listed as valid resources in the laws, meaning the world will refuse their consumption. (the description says: "graphite is mined in Sri Lanka and mixed with clay into leads") lead material renewal: This process attempts to conjure graphite and clay to keep the chain running, but because they are not defined as resources in the laws, the world will refuse the additions. (the description says: "graphite is mined in Sri Lanka and mixed with clay") pack pencil boxes: The move consumes unboxed pencils and empty boxes to produce boxed pencils, but unboxed pencils and empty boxes are not defined as resources in the laws, so the transaction will be refused. (the description says: "packs them into boxes") nothing in the rules: While there is a mechanic to load boxes onto trucks, there is no law authorizing the transfer of boxed pencils from the fac