ays": "The total number of logs changes only when cedar is cut or logs are sawn into slats.", "resource": "logs", "may_change_by": ["cut-cedar", "saw-slats"]}, {"law_id": "slats-flow", "says": "The total number of slats changes only when logs are sawn into slats or slats are assembled into pencils.", "resource": "slats", "may_change_by": ["saw-slats", "assemble-pencils"]}, {"law_id": "leads-flow", "says": "The total number of leads changes only when leads are made or assembled into pencils.", "resource": "leads", "may_change_by": ["make-leads", "assemble-pencils"]}, {"law_id": "boxed-pencils-flow", "says": "The total number of boxed pencils changes only when pencils are packed into boxes or purchased by customers.", "resource": "boxed-pencils", "may_change_by": ["pack-pencils", "sell-boxes"]}, {"law_id": "logs-purchase", "says": "Buying logs transfers logs from the seller to the buyer and pays the seller from the buyer's cash.", "move": "buy-logs", "gives": {"resource": "logs", "from": "seller", "to": "buyer"}, "pays": {"resource": "cash", "from": "buyer", "to": "seller"}}, {"law_id": "slats-purchase", "says": "Buying slats transfers slats from the seller to the buyer and pays the seller from the buyer's cash.", "move": "buy-slats", "gives": {"resource": "slats", "from": "seller", "to": "buyer"}, "pays": {"resource": "cash", "from": "buyer", "to": "seller"}}, {"law_id": "leads-purchase", "says": "Buying leads transfers leads from the seller to the buyer and pays the seller from the buyer's cash.", "move": "buy-leads", "gives": {"resource": "leads", "from": "seller", "to": "buyer"}, "pays": {"resource": "cash", "from": "buyer", "to": "seller"}}, {"law_id": "boxes-purchase", "says": "The shop's purchase of boxed pencils transfers them from the carrier to the shop and pays the carrier from the shop's cash.", "move": "buy-boxes", "gives": {"resource": "boxed-pencils", "from": "seller", "to": "buyer"}, "pays": {"resource": "cash", "from": "buyer", "to": "seller"}}, {"law_id": "customer-sale", "says": "A sale transfers boxed pencils from the shop to the customer and pays the shop from the customer's cash.", "move": "sell-boxes", "gives": {"resource": "boxed-pencils", "from": "shop", "to": "customer"}, "pays": {"resource": "cash", "from": "customer", "to": "shop"}}]}", "role": "assistant"}, {"content": "Rules were written for that structure and test-run, and this is what happened: A separate check read your rules against the description and the laws and found: assemble pencil units: The move consumes paint, erasers, and ferrules and produces unboxed pencils, but none of these are defined as resources in the world's laws, so the move will be refused. (the description says: "paints them and adds erasers and brass ferrules") nothing in the rules: The chain is supposed to keep running, but there is no rule or process that supplies the factory with paint, erasers, ferrules, or empty boxes, meaning the factory will eventually halt. (the description says: "paints them and adds erasers and brass ferrules, packs them into boxes") make leads from materials: The move consumes graphite and clay, which are not listed as valid resources in the laws, meaning the world will refuse their consumption. (the description says: "graphite is mined in Sri Lanka and mixed with clay into leads") lead material renewal: This process attempts to conjure graphite and clay to keep the chain running, but because they are not defined as resources in the laws, the world will refuse the additions. (the description says: "graphite is mined in Sri Lanka and mixed with clay") pack pencil boxes: The move consumes unboxed pencils and empty boxes to produce boxed pencils, but unboxed pencils and empty boxes are not defined as resources in the laws, so the transaction will be refused. (the description says: "packs them into boxes") nothing in the rules: While there is a mechanic to load boxes onto trucks, there is no law authorizing the transfer of boxed pencils from the factory to the carrier, so the move will be refused. (the description says: "trucks deliver the boxes to shops") Fix each of these. In the 24-round test these actors stopped being able to do anything (or never could): pencil-shop (refused: buy-boxes: The carrier has enough boxed pencils: was 5, needed 100, sell-boxes: The shop has a box to sell: was 0, needed 1, buy-boxes: The carrier has enough boxed pencils: was 4, needed 100). Every actor role must be able to act regularly: make sure some actor's action brings what each one's action needs to where it is checked (for example, if a carrier must hold goods before delivering, give another actor an action that loads goods onto the carrier, or let the carrier pick them up itself). A process may renew raw materials at their source or bring new demand, but never supply what an action makes or move goods between places. In the 24-round test these moves were never possible for anyone: sell-boxes (The shop has a box to sell: was 0, needed 1; shop_stock.boxed_pencils is raised only by buy-boxes (on its buyer)). For each, make sure some other action produces what its checks need (for example, if goods must be at the next stop before they can move on, give someone an action that brings them there). Rules can only change the actor and the entities its fields name, and cannot add actions or fields. Return a corrected structure (JSON object only) whose actions and fields let every step and every actor happen, keeping what already worked. Keep the world's resources and laws, updated for every action you add, rename or change: a move that makes or uses up a resource belongs in that law's may_change_by, and a trade its pairing law names must still exist.", "role": "user"}], "prompt_ref": null, "control": {"timeout": 0, "num_retries": 1, "reasoning_effort": "low", "api_base": null, "base_delay": 1.0, "max_delay": 30.0, "retry_on": null, "fallback_models": null, "manual_fallback": null, "execution_mode": "text", "structured_output_mode":